WEBVTT

00:00:00.748 --> 00:00:03.335
Now, listen up. This is a big job.

00:00:03.335 --> 00:00:04.543
The biggest.

00:00:04.543 --> 00:00:06.713
It's the kind of job that if we pull off,

00:00:06.713 --> 00:00:10.467
we won't have to worry about feeding ourselves ever again.

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:12.927
But it comes with a fair bit of risk.

00:00:12.927 --> 00:00:15.096
Once every so often,

00:00:15.096 --> 00:00:17.474
all the farmers in the valley gather together.

00:00:17.474 --> 00:00:20.519
Get out of here! They're angry, nasty.

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:22.729
They want to get their food off the land

00:00:22.729 --> 00:00:24.439
just so we can't have it.

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:27.734
The sweetest corn, the crunchiest carrots,

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:29.736
the ripest radishes.

00:00:29.736 --> 00:00:31.029
[FARMER GRUNTS]

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:32.364
And they bring it all

00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:34.241
to one central location,

00:00:34.241 --> 00:00:35.700
right here in the city,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:36.910
where they guard it

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:38.661
from dawn till dusk.

00:00:38.661 --> 00:00:40.830
And that's where we're gonna hit.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.457
Must be really hard to break in.

00:00:42.457 --> 00:00:44.543
Not a gate or a door in sight.

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:46.294
They wave you in with a smile.

00:00:46.294 --> 00:00:48.255
Come on in. Everybody's welcome.

00:00:48.255 --> 00:00:50.257
Won't they hear us? No.

00:00:50.257 --> 00:00:53.843
There's a band playing wildly mediocre folk music.

00:00:53.843 --> 00:00:56.430
[PLAYING UPBEAT FOLK TUNE]

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.391
What if kids see us? Won't they try and adopt us again?

00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:02.060
In this place, they just give you a little tickle.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:04.854
And if you want an overpriced gift that'll never be used...

00:01:04.854 --> 00:01:07.815
MITTENS: They sell lavender-scented bath bombs.

00:01:07.815 --> 00:01:09.192
Ten pounds. Oh.

00:01:09.192 --> 00:01:11.528
What is this magical place?

00:01:11.528 --> 00:01:15.490
They call it the "farmers market."

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:19.578
Which Whiskers has meticulously recreated here in this map.

00:01:19.578 --> 00:01:21.788
Okay, so the thimbles are fruits.

00:01:21.788 --> 00:01:23.164
Spindles are vegetables.

00:01:23.164 --> 00:01:26.042
The pincushion represents the sun coverage

00:01:26.042 --> 00:01:28.378
according to tomorrow's weather, which I recorded

00:01:28.378 --> 00:01:31.214
over a series of six weekends, not including last Saturday,

00:01:31.214 --> 00:01:32.966
which I deemed unseasonably cloudy.

00:01:32.966 --> 00:01:36.511
Whiskers, no one cares! Oh, all right, fine!

00:01:36.511 --> 00:01:38.597
[GRUNTS]

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:42.434
I hope you guys aren't visual learners.

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:44.852
But the produce ain't what we're after.

00:01:44.852 --> 00:01:47.397
Any chump with a stump can steal that.

00:01:47.397 --> 00:01:50.442
What we want is far more valuable.

00:01:50.442 --> 00:01:52.444
Deep in the middle of all this,

00:01:52.444 --> 00:01:53.861
across from the coconut water

00:01:53.861 --> 00:01:56.197
and two down from the wooden spoons,

00:01:56.197 --> 00:01:57.865
are the crown jewels.

00:01:57.865 --> 00:02:01.620
Our target: the dried fruit.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.539
Huh? Dried fruit? Ew.

00:02:04.539 --> 00:02:06.416
Why would you want that? Sounds gross.

00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:07.875
[SNAPS]

00:02:08.918 --> 00:02:10.295
Lasts forever,

00:02:10.295 --> 00:02:12.088
and it's only one-eighth the size

00:02:12.088 --> 00:02:13.672
of a piece of fresh fruit.

00:02:13.672 --> 00:02:16.217
But with the same nutritional value.

00:02:16.217 --> 00:02:19.762
It's easy to transport and totally untraceable.

00:02:19.762 --> 00:02:22.432
TOM: Try that.

00:02:22.432 --> 00:02:24.184
Yum! That's so good.

00:02:24.184 --> 00:02:26.269
Pfft, it's no jelly bean.

00:02:26.269 --> 00:02:28.188
Hey! We don't do that stuff here.

00:02:28.188 --> 00:02:30.731
Get me, kid? Junks up your noggin.

00:02:30.731 --> 00:02:34.693
Problem is, the dried fruit is in the center of the market,

00:02:34.693 --> 00:02:37.155
surrounded by all the farmers.

00:02:37.155 --> 00:02:39.199
SAMUEL: And the worst thing about farmers,

00:02:39.199 --> 00:02:42.577
they stick together, protect each other.

00:02:42.577 --> 00:02:44.496
BARNABAS: And they are an evil army

00:02:44.496 --> 00:02:46.914
evilly unified in evil.

00:02:46.914 --> 00:02:48.667
But even if we take care of them,

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.085
we've got to get past the toughest one of all.

00:02:51.085 --> 00:02:53.421
The dried fruit vendor herself,

00:02:53.421 --> 00:02:56.466
Sara Nakamoto.

00:02:56.466 --> 00:02:59.678
Never leaves her post, no matter what.

00:02:59.678 --> 00:03:02.681
But Sara Nakamoto has one Achilles' heel.

00:03:02.681 --> 00:03:05.308
And it's not her actual Achilles' heel.

00:03:05.308 --> 00:03:09.312
Her proverbial Achilles' heel is the son of the cheesemonger

00:03:09.312 --> 00:03:12.023
across the aisle, William Pemberly.

00:03:12.023 --> 00:03:14.901
He's the only one who can get her attention.

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:17.696
So if we get to him, he'll distract her,

00:03:17.696 --> 00:03:20.156
and the dried fruit will be ours.

00:03:20.156 --> 00:03:22.783
How do we get it out of there? Our old friend upstairs

00:03:22.783 --> 00:03:26.871
comes to market every week, just before it closes.

00:03:26.871 --> 00:03:29.040
He always buys two sausages.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.750
One for him and one for his late wife.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.878
It's a real love story, actually.

00:03:33.878 --> 00:03:36.464
They met as teenagers at a jazz hall.

00:03:36.464 --> 00:03:39.342
She was a hat-check girl. He played the horn.

00:03:39.342 --> 00:03:40.968
But their parents didn't approve.

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:43.096
Whiskers! Whiskers, stay focused.

00:03:43.096 --> 00:03:46.391
Ugh! Why doesn't anyone appreciate a good digression?

00:03:46.391 --> 00:03:48.351
Know what they'll say at your funeral?

00:03:48.351 --> 00:03:51.563
"Great lady. Always stayed on topic."

00:03:53.648 --> 00:03:56.817
Anyway, we haul the loot into the tailor's truck,

00:03:56.817 --> 00:03:59.320
and he drives it right back here for us, okay?

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.239
[LAUGHING] [ALL CHEERING]

00:04:01.239 --> 00:04:03.116
It all seems very complicated.

00:04:03.116 --> 00:04:06.536
Which is why I said I wish I had 10 more like you.

00:04:06.536 --> 00:04:09.664
Have any friends back home? Yes, we have lots of friends.

00:04:09.664 --> 00:04:12.542
Can they be trusted? Um, there's a couple

00:04:12.542 --> 00:04:13.834
I wouldn't let house-sit.

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:16.379
It doesn't matter. Bring them all.

00:04:16.379 --> 00:04:18.965
[MATT AND KIM'S "COME TOGETHER NOW" PLAYING]

00:04:21.426 --> 00:04:22.843
♪ Come together now ♪

00:04:22.843 --> 00:04:24.220
Hm?

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:28.224
♪ Come together now Square to a hexagon ♪

00:04:28.224 --> 00:04:29.684
[GIGGLES]

00:04:29.684 --> 00:04:32.353
♪ Pepsi, Coke And then you mix a little ice ♪

00:04:32.353 --> 00:04:34.021
♪ Street signs in camouflage ♪

00:04:34.021 --> 00:04:35.189
[SHOUTS]

00:04:35.189 --> 00:04:37.233
♪ Got no time to waste ♪

00:04:37.233 --> 00:04:39.152
[LAUGHS]

00:04:39.152 --> 00:04:40.737
♪ You're a mess ♪

00:04:40.737 --> 00:04:42.280
[GRUNTING GOOFILY]

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.783
♪ Loosen up a bit Flex and take the hit ♪

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:46.326
PETER: Come on, Felix, let's go.

00:04:46.326 --> 00:04:48.161
♪ Let's come together now ♪

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.625
Come on, Felix, let's go.

00:04:57.253 --> 00:04:59.673
Girls, go and get a flashlight. Okay.

00:04:59.673 --> 00:05:01.508
♪ Come together now ♪

00:05:03.301 --> 00:05:05.595
[ALL PANTING]

00:05:05.595 --> 00:05:07.472
[GRUNTING]

00:05:11.225 --> 00:05:13.812
All right, everyone. I think these are ready

00:05:13.812 --> 00:05:15.355
to sell at the farmers market.

00:05:15.355 --> 00:05:17.691
I want honest opinions from everyone. Right?

00:05:17.691 --> 00:05:21.277
Don't hold back. I need to know the truth, but...

00:05:21.277 --> 00:05:22.654
only if it's good. Heh.

00:05:22.654 --> 00:05:24.238
So really sock it to me.

00:05:24.238 --> 00:05:26.783
But remember, I'm wildly insecure.

00:05:26.783 --> 00:05:28.284
Hm. ALL: Mm-hm.

00:05:28.284 --> 00:05:30.829
Oh, you've actually put them on the beach.

00:05:30.829 --> 00:05:32.997
BEA: Mm, I'm just expanding our world.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:34.791
You've expanded it

00:05:34.791 --> 00:05:36.250
all the way to outer space.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.002
Mm-hm. Nigel wants me to--

00:05:38.002 --> 00:05:40.755
I know what Nigel wants. Is it...?

00:05:40.755 --> 00:05:42.465
Is it what you want?

00:05:42.465 --> 00:05:45.552
It feels like you're jamming in everything here in a way that--

00:05:45.552 --> 00:05:48.095
Jam jars. Pardon me?

00:05:48.095 --> 00:05:50.973
For their space helmets. It's perfect.

00:05:50.973 --> 00:05:53.976
Just shove it on. Little head, the ears down.

00:05:53.976 --> 00:05:56.354
Show what it does to the face. It's perfect.

00:05:58.481 --> 00:06:00.775
Oh... THOMAS: Nigel Basil-Jones.

00:06:00.775 --> 00:06:04.445
Just because he's successful, intelligent, charismatic,

00:06:04.445 --> 00:06:06.406
eyes you could lose an afternoon in...

00:06:06.406 --> 00:06:07.490
[CHUCKLES, SNORTS]

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:09.701
He needs to hear from me.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.786
You lot, stay out of trouble.

00:06:11.786 --> 00:06:13.954
Although, I guess I don't need to say that

00:06:13.954 --> 00:06:15.956
because Peter's not here. Heh.

00:06:15.956 --> 00:06:17.542
Where is Peter?

00:06:19.168 --> 00:06:22.505
Once again, I find myself talking to rabbits. Heh.

00:06:22.505 --> 00:06:24.883
Expecting a response, which...

00:06:27.218 --> 00:06:30.304
No. It's not forthcoming. Okay.

00:06:30.304 --> 00:06:33.433
[FLOPSY & MOPSY WHIMPERING]

00:06:33.433 --> 00:06:35.518
[STEAM HISSING] [BOTH SIGH]

00:06:35.518 --> 00:06:37.228
[PETER SIGHS]

00:06:38.897 --> 00:06:41.524
Flashlight.

00:06:41.524 --> 00:06:43.818
And for our British friends...

00:06:43.818 --> 00:06:46.404
Torch.

